{"id": "EUVD-2026-86246", "enisaUuid": "09fd7a37-03e3-3e18-8ad5-91700f3e138a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmemcg: make the v1 soft limit knob inert\n\nThe v1 soft limit has been deprecated since v6.12 and nobody has reported\ndepending on it.  Start the removal by decoupling the interface from the\nimplementation: keep memory.soft_limit_in_bytes, but ignore writes to it\nand always report the maximum value on read similar to what\nmemory.kmem.limit_in_bytes already does.\n\nWrites are still parsed, so malformed input keeps returning -EINVAL.  The\nknob now also behaves the same everywhere: it used to return -EOPNOTSUPP\non PREEMPT_RT, where soft limit reclaim has always been disabled.\n\nThis also fixes the syzbot report linked below.  Soft limit reclaim is the\nonly caller that runs shrink_lruvec() from kswapd against a specific\nmemcg, so it is the only way to reach lru_gen_shrink_lruvec() and in turn\nset_mm_walk(), which warns when called from kswapd.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:34:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:27", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf75f14d755f9cfbb246e6cc011b53cdd5142de3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72fb67f6e0e5d78e4f34cf9929d1afdb0fd54203", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a90e268cce7023f34087bfa4affb42e29ff5f45", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5ec8f629a300cc40e746d6178f724bdff7683fa7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a3417097fb107cea3358b19bcbb4eb655fd67f8c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xfgg-2xcm-vrc8", "CVE-2026-93240"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "003a9331-3752-3320-9c85-0c683b4f8a49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "11e3ee85-379d-35ef-9609-163907461e57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e9d4e1ee788097484606c32122f146d802a9c5fb <0a90e268cce7023f34087bfa4affb42e29ff5f45"}, {"id": "179c27de-66c3-3646-a9a1-829f076e8c0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e9d4e1ee788097484606c32122f146d802a9c5fb <5ec8f629a300cc40e746d6178f724bdff7683fa7"}, {"id": "246286b5-bed8-3120-b9b1-6741e459e0df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e9d4e1ee788097484606c32122f146d802a9c5fb <bf75f14d755f9cfbb246e6cc011b53cdd5142de3"}, {"id": "250cb050-b716-371d-a101-349f56cc3490", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.3"}, {"id": "2758dbc2-47b0-3e40-993d-24f2c6f6dad0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e9d4e1ee788097484606c32122f146d802a9c5fb <a3417097fb107cea3358b19bcbb4eb655fd67f8c"}, {"id": "5d7975da-07a3-3445-ba8d-dbaf4ad67592", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6b4922b3-39ff-3793-8dae-7e6188fbbf7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "a135f7a8-a958-3e4c-bfb0-e503ee226d5a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "e4eb7aeb-cd3f-33cd-b7c3-44090b4d0940", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e9d4e1ee788097484606c32122f146d802a9c5fb <72fb67f6e0e5d78e4f34cf9929d1afdb0fd54203"}, {"id": "f0a9f39e-5c70-31cb-83ae-bf400267d77c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "ffe865e0-c57c-396f-acab-ec5c29b68ee6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2908c90e-d071-39e1-b24a-72c3041e8ae3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}